{com}. do "W:\Mac_Sync\Desktop\public_release_science_20260904\analytics\CNKI\02_public_listed_firms.do"
{txt}
{com}. /*******************************************************************************
> Project: CNKI analysis
> Script:  02_public_listed_firms.do
> 
> Purpose:
>   Estimate baseline difference-in-differences (DID) models for publication
>   outcomes among Chinese listed firms. Results compare the full sample with a
>   coarsened-exact-matching (CEM) sample using level, log-transformed, and Poisson
>   specifications.
> 
> Main inputs:
>   - ${c -(}stata_output{c )-}CNKI_listedfirm_DID.dta (full listed-firm sample)
>   - ${c -(}stata_output{c )-}CNKI_listedfirm_DID_cem.dta (CEM sample and weights)
> 
> Main output:
>   ${c -(}table_output{c )-}CNKI_listedfirm.rtf
> 
> Required setup:
>   00_run_all.do defines stata_output and table_output before calling this file.
>   The global macro $controls must be defined by the calling environment. The
>   script also requires the community-contributed commands reghdfe, ppmlhdfe,
>   and esttab.
> *******************************************************************************/
. 
. * ==============================================================================
. * 1. Estimate models for the full listed-firm sample
. * ==============================================================================
. 
. use ${c -(}stata_output{c )-}CNKI_listedfirm_DID.dta, clear
{txt}
{com}. 
. global controls cash RDSpendSumRatio ROA AssetLiabilityRatio TobinQ academic_experience
{txt}
{com}. 
. * Model 1: linear specification for winsorized publication counts.
. reghdfe pub_num_w did $controls, absorb(Symbol_id year) vce(r)
{res}{txt}(dropped 63 {browse "http://scorreia.com/research/singletons.pdf":singleton observations})
{res}{txt}({browse "http://scorreia.com/research/hdfe.pdf":MWFE estimator} converged in 2 iterations)
